<%#
  Cross-environment sync banner. Shows on the LOCAL (development) side
  only — production is a read-mostly environment whose admin shouldn't
  be nagged about sync state on every page render. The Site Sync page
  on prod still surfaces the same info for anyone who wants to check.

  Authority: SiteSync::Conclusion, the one answer shared with the nav
  dot, the imports publish panel and the Site Sync page. We don't trust
  local-ledger drift as a sync signal because the ledger can get
  rewritten by paths that didn't actually transfer content.

  States:
    - in sync          → hidden
    - out of sync      → "local differs from live, sync to align"
    - unknown          → hidden unless the peer is unreachable; the peer
                         answer is older than our last sync, so a refresh
                         is already enqueued and any warning here would
                         be about content we've since sent. The Site Sync
                         page says so out loud instead.
    - peer unreachable → "live unreachable, content can't be verified"
%>
<% if Rails.env.development? %>
  <% conclusion = local_assigns[:conclusion] || @sync_conclusion || SiteSync::Conclusion.current %>

  <% if !conclusion.configured %>
    <%# No peer URL or token configured — nothing to compare to. Silent. %>

  <% elsif conclusion.in_sync? %>
    <%# Happy path — nothing to surface. %>

  <% elsif !conclusion.peer_reachable %>
    <div class="admin-warning-bar bg-amber-100 border-l-4 border-amber-500 text-amber-900 p-4 font-mono text-xs">
      <p>
        🔌 Live site is unreachable. Local content can't be verified as in sync —
        there appear to be unsynced changes. Restore the connection to live and sync.
        <% unless request.path == admin_site_sync_path %>
          <%= link_to "Open Site Sync →", admin_site_sync_path, class: "underline" %>
        <% end %>
      </p>
    </div>

  <% elsif conclusion.undecided? %>
    <%# Peer answered before our last sync — a background refresh is on its
        way, and claiming drift here is the bug this replaced. %>

  <% else %>
    <div class="admin-warning-bar bg-amber-100 border-l-4 border-amber-500 text-amber-900 p-4 font-mono text-xs">
      <p>
        🔄 Local content differs from live. Sync to align both sides.
        <% unless request.path == admin_site_sync_path %>
          <%= link_to "Open Site Sync →", admin_site_sync_path, class: "underline" %>
        <% end %>
      </p>
    </div>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
